    "starterCode": "def check_rate_limit(request_timestamps, window_seconds=60, max_requests=5):\n    # Return True if allowed, False if blocked\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "check_rate_limit([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 55], 60, 5) == False",
    "solution": "def check_rate_limit(request_timestamps, window_seconds=60, max_requests=5):\n    if not request_timestamps: return True\n    current_time = request_timestamps[-1]\n    recent = [t for t in request_timestamps if current_time - t <= window_seconds]\n    return len(recent) <= max_requests",
    "explanation": "Implements sliding window rate limiter against automated brute force.",
