    "question": "Write a JavaScript function `isLikelySqlInjection(paramValue)` that returns true if a URL parameter value contains common SQL injection payload patterns like single quotes, comment dashes, or 'OR 1=1'.",
    "starterCode": "function isLikelySqlInjection(paramValue) {\n  // your code here\n}",
    "expectedOutput": "true",
    "solution": "function isLikelySqlInjection(paramValue) {\n  const decoded = decodeURIComponent(paramValue);\n  const pattern = /('|\"|;|--|\\/\\*|union\\s+select|or\\s+1=1)/i;\n  return pattern.test(decoded);\n}",
    "explanation": "Decodes the parameter string and tests against common SQLi syntax tokens and tautology strings."
