    "question": "Write a JavaScript function `extractIpAddresses(logText)` that extracts all unique IPv4 addresses found in an arbitrary log message string.",
    "starterCode": "function extractIpAddresses(logText) {\n  // your code here\n}",
    "expectedOutput": "[\"10.0.0.1\", \"192.168.1.5\"]",
    "solution": "function extractIpAddresses(logText) {\n  const regex = /\\b(?:\\d{1,3}\\.){3}\\d{1,3}\\b/g;\n  const matches = logText.match(regex) || [];\n  // Filter valid IP byte values (0-255)\n  const valid = matches.filter(ip => {\n    return ip.split('.').every(num => {\n      const n = parseInt(num, 10);\n      return n >= 0 && n <= 255;\n    });\n  });\n  return Array.from(new Set(valid));\n}",
    "explanation": "Finds all candidate IPv4 patterns via regex, validates that each octet is 0-255, and dedupes the results."
