    "question": "Write a JavaScript function `scanForLeakedKeys(fileContent)` that returns an array of potential AWS Access Key IDs found in a text file (matching regex `\\b(AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16})\\b`).",
    "starterCode": "function scanForLeakedKeys(fileContent) {\n  // your code here\n}",
    "expectedOutput": "[\"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\"]",
    "solution": "function scanForLeakedKeys(fileContent) {\n  const regex = /\\b(AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16})\\b/g;\n  const matches = fileContent.match(regex) || [];\n  return Array.from(new Set(matches));\n}",
