    "question": "Write a JavaScript function `parseVpcFlowLog(line)` that parses a VPC Flow Log line string formatted as `\"version account-id interface-id srcaddr dstaddr srcport dstport protocol packets bytes start end action log-status\"` and returns an object `{ srcAddr, dstAddr, srcPort, dstPort, action }`.",
    "starterCode": "function parseVpcFlowLog(line) {\n  // your code here\n}",
    "expectedOutput": "{\"srcAddr\": \"10.0.0.5\", \"dstAddr\": \"198.51.100.2\", \"srcPort\": 443, \"dstPort\": 49152, \"action\": \"ACCEPT\"}",
    "solution": "function parseVpcFlowLog(line) {\n  const parts = line.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n  if (parts.length < 14) return null;\n  return {\n    srcAddr: parts[3],\n    dstAddr: parts[4],\n    srcPort: parseInt(parts[5], 10),\n    dstPort: parseInt(parts[6], 10),\n    action: parts[12]\n  };\n}",
    "explanation": "Extracts key fields from standard default format AWS VPC Flow Log lines."
