    "starterCode": "import asyncio\n\nasync def bounded_gather(tasks: list, max_concurrency: int = 3) -> list:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 3]",
    "solution": "import asyncio\n\nasync def bounded_gather(tasks: list, max_concurrency: int = 3) -> list:\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrency)\n    async def worker(task):\n        async with sem:\n            return await task\n    return await asyncio.gather(*(worker(t) for t in tasks))",
    "explanation": "Wraps coroutines in semaphore context blocks to ensure no more than `max_concurrency` calls run in parallel."
