    "question": "Write a Python class `InMemoryVectorStore` that stores items `{'id': str, 'text': str, 'vector': list[float]}` and provides `search(query_vector, top_k=2)` calculating dot product similarity and returning top_k texts.",
    "starterCode": "class InMemoryVectorStore:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "['doc1', 'doc2']",
    "solution": "class InMemoryVectorStore:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.items = []\n    def add(self, item_id: str, text: str, vector: list[float]):\n        self.items.append({'id': item_id, 'text': text, 'vector': vector})\n    def search(self, query_vector: list[float], top_k: int = 2) -> list[str]:\n        def dot_product(v1, v2):\n            return sum(a * b for a, b in zip(v1, v2))\n        scored = [(dot_product(it['vector'], query_vector), it['text']) for it in self.items]\n        scored.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n        return [text for _, text in scored[:top_k]]",
    "explanation": "Implements basic in-memory vector storage and top-k dot product retrieval."
