    "expectedOutput": "{'added': ['y'], 'modified': ['x'], 'removed': ['z']}",
    "solution": "def diff_agent_states(old_state: dict, new_state: dict) -> dict:\n    old_keys, new_keys = set(old_state.keys()), set(new_state.keys())\n    added = sorted(list(new_keys - old_keys))\n    removed = sorted(list(old_keys - new_keys))\n    modified = sorted([k for k in (old_keys & new_keys) if old_state[k] != new_state[k]])\n    return {'added': added, 'modified': modified, 'removed': removed}",
    "explanation": "Detects state mutations between consecutive checkpoints for debugging and tracing."
