    "question": "Write a Python class `HybridWorkflowFSM` with states `['INTAKE', 'REASONING', 'VALIDATION', 'COMPLETE']`. Provide `transition(next_state)` which only permits sequential transitions from `INTAKE -> REASONING -> VALIDATION -> COMPLETE` or `VALIDATION -> REASONING`.",
    "starterCode": "class HybridWorkflowFSM:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "True",
    "solution": "class HybridWorkflowFSM:\n    VALID_TRANSITIONS = {\n        'INTAKE': ['REASONING'],\n        'REASONING': ['VALIDATION'],\n        'VALIDATION': ['COMPLETE', 'REASONING'],\n        'COMPLETE': []\n    }\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.current_state = 'INTAKE'\n    def transition(self, next_state: str) -> bool:\n        if next_state in self.VALID_TRANSITIONS.get(self.current_state, []):\n            self.current_state = next_state\n            return True\n        return False",
    "explanation": "Implements finite state machine governing allowable transitions in hybrid workflows."
