    "starterCode": "def custom_list_append_reducer(current_list: list[str], new_items: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "['a', 'b', 'c']",
    "solution": "def custom_list_append_reducer(current_list: list[str], new_items: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    seen = set(current_list)\n    result = list(current_list)\n    for item in new_items:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            result.append(item)\n    return result",
    "explanation": "Custom state reducer function enforcing deduplication on list channel updates."
