    "question": "Write a Python function `calculate_pass_at_k(n, c, k)` that calculates Pass@k metric: `1 - [comb(n - c, k) / comb(n, k)]` where `n` is total generated samples, `c` is number of correct samples, and `k` is evaluation sample size.",
    "starterCode": "import math\n\ndef calculate_pass_at_k(n: int, c: int, k: int) -> float:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "0.8",
    "solution": "import math\n\ndef calculate_pass_at_k(n: int, c: int, k: int) -> float:\n    if n - c < k:\n        return 1.0\n    return 1.0 - (math.comb(n - c, k) / math.comb(n, k))",
    "explanation": "Implements the standard unbiased Pass@k formula used in code generation benchmarks."
