    "question": "Write a Python class `SkillLibraryVectorIndex` with `add_skill(skill_name, code_snippet, embedding)` and `retrieve_skill(query_embedding, top_k=1)` using dot-product similarity, returning list of skill names.",
    "starterCode": "class SkillLibraryVectorIndex:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "['mine_wood']",
    "solution": "class SkillLibraryVectorIndex:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.skills = []\n    def add_skill(self, skill_name: str, code_snippet: str, embedding: list[float]):\n        self.skills.append({'name': skill_name, 'code': code_snippet, 'embedding': embedding})\n    def retrieve_skill(self, query_embedding: list[float], top_k: int = 1) -> list[str]:\n        def dot(v1, v2): return sum(a * b for a, b in zip(v1, v2))\n        ranked = sorted(self.skills, key=lambda s: dot(s['embedding'], query_embedding), reverse=True)\n        return [s['name'] for s in ranked[:top_k]]",
    "explanation": "Replicates Voyager's self-expanding skill library retrieval mechanism."
