    "question": "Write a Python function `compute_faithfulness_score(claims, reference_text)` where claims is a list of statement strings. Returns `float` (supported claims / total claims) where a claim is considered supported if all its words exist in `reference_text` (case-insensitive).",
    "starterCode": "def compute_faithfulness_score(claims: list[str], reference_text: str) -> float:\n    # your code here\n    pass",
    "expectedOutput": "1.0",
    "solution": "def compute_faithfulness_score(claims: list[str], reference_text: str) -> float:\n    if not claims: return 1.0\n    ref_words = set(reference_text.lower().split())\n    supported = 0\n    for claim in claims:\n        claim_words = set(claim.lower().split())\n        if claim_words.issubset(ref_words):\n            supported += 1\n    return round(supported / len(claims), 2)",
    "explanation": "Calculates simple lexical grounding faithfulness score for RAG evaluation."
